// D-COMPILER-INPUT-PROPORTIONAL-RECURSION-RESIDUE-UNCONVERTED-AND-UNCAPPED
// (P61, lane ml): a RUNNABLE witness for the MIR tier's half of the row -- the
// `SeqExpr` comma chain, its by-ADDRESS twin, the `*&` request rewrite and the
// `BuiltinCall` argument pump, all of which now cost HEAP rather than host call
// frames in `src/mir/lowering/hir_to_mir.cpp`.
//
// *** WHAT THIS FILE PROVES AT RUNTIME IS **ORDER**, AND THAT IS THE HALF A
// FLATTENING MOST EASILY BREAKS. A comma chain's whole meaning is the sequence
// its side effects run in; a work-stack rewrite that drained the statements in
// the wrong order, dropped one, or ran one twice would still compile, still link
// and still exit -- with a different number. So every element below alternates
// `a *= M` with `a -= K`, and multiplication does not commute with subtraction:
// swapping ANY two adjacent elements changes the answer.
//
// *** AND THE COMMA CHAIN IS CHECKED AGAINST A SECOND MACHINE. `comma_chain`
// and `stmt_list` compute the identical arithmetic, but they reach MIR through
// DIFFERENT drivers: the comma is a left-nested `SeqExpr` tower whose side
// effects run through the value driver's statement pump, while the statement
// list is one `Block` frame walking a child cursor. They agree only if the comma
// machine runs its statements in source order, so this is a differential test,
// not a golden.
//
// ANTI-FOLD: the accumulator starts from a MUTABLE GLOBAL and the `*&` chain
// walks a MUTABLE GLOBAL pointer, so no front-end arm can fold either away and
// report green without having lowered it.
//
// (i) HONEST SCOPE, stated rather than implied. This file does not, and cannot,
// exercise the CEILING that moved. `dsscp` builds every CU inside a 64 MiB
// worker (`substrate::kDeepRecursionStackBytes`), so the pre-P61 compiler also
// accepted these depths through the CLI; the ceiling itself is pinned IN
// PROCESS, on a 256 KiB bounded stack, by
// `tests/mir/test_deep_nesting_costs_heap.cpp` -- which is where a regression to
// host recursion goes red under the gate's own toolchain. What this file adds is
// the runtime half: that the flattened lowering still MEANS what C says. The
// 1000-element comma chain is also ~3x the depth at which the pre-P61 lowering
// died on an ORDINARY 1 MiB thread (MEASURED 320 rc 0 / 340 stack death), which
// is the budget a library embedder or the LSP gets -- neither of those goes
// through the CLI's large-stack worker.
//
// (i) AND WHAT BOUNDS THE CHAIN HERE IS NO LONGER THIS TIER. MEASURED through
// `dsscp` ON THIS EXACT ELEMENT SHAPE (an earlier note quoted 800/1600, which
// were taken on a DIFFERENT shape -- `a = a*M + K` -- and so said nothing about
// the file that ships): a chain of these alternating elements compiles at 1000
// and at 1150 (rc 0), and is REFUSED LOUD at 1175 and above with a positioned
// `P_SpeculationBudgetExhausted` naming `parser.speculationBudgetFactor`. That
// is the parser's per-alternative token budget, whose value is held down by an
// O(depth) builder/schema-walker checkpoint -- a performance property recorded
// on this row, not a MIR-tier recursion. A loud refusal is the outcome the
// standing ruling asks for; a stack death was not.
//
// *** SO THE MARGIN IS ~15%, AND IT IS STATED BECAUSE IT IS SMALL. The 1000
// shipped here is about 15% under the 1175 that refuses today. Shrinking the
// per-alternative token budget, or the O(depth) checkpoint that holds it down,
// flips this example from exit 42 to a COMPILE REFUSAL -- and the gate would
// then red on an example rather than on the change that caused it. Anyone moving
// either knob re-measures this number first. What the file PROVES is order, not
// depth (the depth ceiling is pinned in-process, above), so the length is free
// to come down if that margin is ever spent.
//
// REFERENCE ORACLE, each probed SEPARATELY (rc 0 = compiled, and the three that
// can run it here all RAN it to 42): gcc 13.3.0 and clang 18.1.3 compile and run
// this file at -O0 and -O2; mingw-w64 gcc 13.2.0 compiles and runs it at -O0 and
// -O2; MSVC 19.51.36252 compiles it (`cl /c /std:c17`). On the underlying axes,
// all four references compile a 1000-element comma chain and a 1000-statement block
// (all four reach 16000, and gcc and MSVC reach 65536); 600 `*&` pairs and 200
// nested `__builtin_popcount` calls are inside every reference's working range
// too -- clang refuses more than 256 brackets LOUDLY, so 200 is its last working
// builtin depth. The `release` arm additionally proves the result survives
// Mem2Reg/CSE/LICM/DCE with the same exit code.
//
// exit = 12 + 10 + 8 + 6 + 6 = 42.

unsigned gseed = 1u;
int gx = 7;
